<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Bastion report: {{ ctx.logfile }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0d1117; --panel: #161b22; --border: #30363d;
    --text: #c9d1d9; --muted: #8b949e;
    --critical: #ff5555; --high: #f85149; --medium: #d29922;
    --low: #58a6ff; --informational: #8b949e;
    --green: #3fb950; --red: #f85149;
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); margin: 0;
         font: 15px/1.5 "Segoe UI", system-ui, sans-serif; }
  .wrap { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px; }
  h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 32px 0 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
       padding-bottom: 6px; }
  h3 { font-size: 15px; margin: 18px 0 8px; color: var(--muted);
       text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .stats { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin: 16px 0; }
  .stat { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px;
          padding: 12px 18px; min-width: 130px; }
  .stat .num { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; }
  .stat .lbl { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  .stat.warn .num { color: var(--red); }
  .banner { background: #2d1d10; border: 1px solid #6b4a1b; border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 10px 14px; margin: 14px 0; color: #e3b341; font-size: 14px; }
  .card { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px;
          padding: 14px 16px; margin: 10px 0; }
  .card .head { display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: baseline; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .card .title { font-weight: 600; }
  .badge { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase;
           border-radius: 10px; padding: 2px 9px; color: #0d1117; }
  .badge.critical { background: var(--critical); }
  .badge.high { background: var(--high); }
  .badge.medium { background: var(--medium); }
  .badge.low { background: var(--low); }
  .badge.informational { background: var(--informational); }
  .tech { color: var(--low); font-size: 13px; }
  .meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 4px; }
  table.evidence { border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 8px; font-size: 13px; width: 100%; }
  table.evidence td { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 4px 8px;
                      font-family: Consolas, monospace; word-break: break-all; }
  table.evidence td.k { color: var(--muted); width: 160px; }
  pre.raw { background: #0b0e13; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px;
            padding: 8px 10px; font: 12px/1.4 Consolas, monospace; overflow-x: auto;
            white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-all; color: var(--muted); margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .bar { background: #21262d; border-radius: 6px; height: 14px; overflow: hidden; }
  .bar .fill { background: var(--green); height: 100%; }
  .tactic-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr 110px; gap: 12px;
                align-items: center; margin: 6px 0; }
  .tactic-row .nums { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; text-align: right; }
  details { margin: 8px 0; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); }
  .chips { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px; margin: 8px 0; }
  .chip { font: 12px Consolas, monospace; border-radius: 4px; padding: 2px 7px;
          border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .chip.ok { color: var(--green); border-color: #238636; }
  .chip.miss { color: var(--red); border-color: #6e2c28; }
  .footer { color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; margin-top: 36px;
            border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding-top: 10px; }
  .timeline { border-left: 2px solid var(--border); margin: 12px 0 12px 6px;
              padding-left: 18px; }
  .trow { position: relative; margin: 10px 0; }
  .trow::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: -23px; top: 6px;
                  width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 50%;
                  background: var(--border); }
  .trow .when { font: 12px Consolas, monospace; color: var(--muted);
                margin-right: 8px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Bastion detection report</h1>
  <div class="sub">
    Log file <strong>{{ ctx.logfile }}</strong> ({{ ctx.platform }}) ·
    Sigma {{ ctx.sigma_version or "(custom rules dir)" }} ·
    ATT&amp;CK {% if ctx.attack_version %}v{{ ctx.attack_version }}{% else %}(custom bundle){% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="stats">
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{{ result.events_scanned }}</div><div class="lbl">events scanned</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{{ result.rules_loaded }}</div><div class="lbl">rules loaded</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{{ result.detections | length }}</div><div class="lbl">detections</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{{ techniques_hit | length }}</div><div class="lbl">techniques observed</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{{ summary.covered_count }}/{{ summary.total_count }}</div><div class="lbl">techniques covered by ruleset</div></div>
    <div class="stat warn"><div class="num">{{ summary.uncovered_gap_count }}</div><div class="lbl">writable gaps: visible in this telemetry, no rule</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{{ summary.uncovered_beyond_telemetry_count }}</div><div class="lbl">uncovered: needs telemetry Bastion does not read</div></div>
    <div class="stat"><div class="num">{{ summary.uncovered_beyond_host_count }}</div><div class="lbl">uncovered: no Windows/Linux component</div></div>
  </div>

  {% if ctx.unsupported_rule_count or ctx.rule_error_count %}
  <div class="banner">
    Caveats: {{ ctx.unsupported_rule_count }} rules use unsupported Sigma grammar and were not
    evaluated; {{ ctx.rule_error_count }} rules errored and were skipped. Neither group counts
    toward coverage.
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if ctx.unresolved_techniques %}
  <div class="banner">
    Technique tags not in this ATT&amp;CK release (deprecated/unknown):
    {{ ctx.unresolved_techniques | join(", ") }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Detections by ATT&amp;CK tactic</h2>
  {% if not result.detections %}
  <p>No detections in this log.</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% for tactic, detections in detection_groups.items() %}
  <h3>{{ tactic }} ({{ detections | length }})</h3>
  {% for detection in detections %}
  <div class="card">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="badge {{ detection.level }}">{{ detection.level }}</span>
      <span class="title">{{ detection.rule_title }}</span>
      <span class="tech">
        {% for ref in detection.techniques %}{{ ref.id }} {{ ref.name }}{% if not loop.last %} · {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="meta">
      {{ detection.event.source }}
      {% if detection.event.timestamp %} · {{ detection.event.timestamp.isoformat() }}{% endif %}
      · rule {{ detection.rule_id }}
    </div>
    <table class="evidence">
      {% for key, value in detection.matched_fields.items() %}
      <tr><td class="k">{{ key }}</td><td>{{ value }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
    <pre class="raw">{{ detection.event.raw }}</pre>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endfor %}

  {% if timeline %}
  <h2>Timeline</h2>
  <div class="timeline">
    {% for detection in timeline %}
    <div class="trow">
      <span class="when">{{ detection.event.timestamp.isoformat() if detection.event.timestamp else "no timestamp" }}</span>
      <span class="badge {{ detection.level }}">{{ detection.level }}</span>
      {{ detection.rule_title }}
      <span class="tech">
        {% for ref in detection.techniques %}{{ ref.id }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </span>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>ATT&amp;CK coverage of the loaded ruleset</h2>
  <p>
    The ruleset references <strong>{{ summary.covered_count }} of {{ summary.total_count }}</strong>
    enterprise techniques. <strong style="color: var(--red)">{{ uncovered_count }} techniques have
    no detection rule at all.</strong> A green chip below means at least one rule is tagged to the
    technique, which is not the same as saying the activity would be detected.
  </p>
  <p>
    The uncovered count splits three ways, using ATT&amp;CK's platform metadata and the log
    sources its detection strategies name.
    <strong>{{ summary.uncovered_beyond_host_count }}</strong> techniques have no Windows or
    Linux component at all: they happen in cloud control planes, identity providers, network
    devices, ESXi, or on the adversary's own infrastructure before a compromise, so no host-log
    scanner could ever observe them.
    <strong>{{ summary.uncovered_beyond_telemetry_count }}</strong> can occur on a host, but
    every detection strategy ATT&amp;CK lists for them relies on telemetry Bastion does not
    read: EDR memory sensors, auditd, eBPF, network monitoring, or macOS sources. The remaining
    <strong style="color: var(--red)">{{ summary.uncovered_gap_count }}</strong> are writable
    gaps: ATT&amp;CK maps them to Windows event logs or Linux syslog, the telemetry this tool
    ingests, and rules in this format could close them. (Techniques without detection-strategy
    metadata are counted as writable, so the gap number never understates the work.) Full
    coverage of this matrix is not an achievable or honest goal for a host-log tool; driving
    the writable-gap count down is.
  </p>
  {% for tactic, buckets in coverage_groups.items() %}
  {% set covered = buckets.covered | length %}
  {% set total = covered + (buckets.uncovered | length) %}
  <div class="tactic-row">
    <div>{{ tactic }}</div>
    <div class="bar"><div class="fill" style="width: {{ (covered / total * 100) | round }}%"></div></div>
    <div class="nums">{{ covered }} / {{ total }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

  <details>
    <summary>Per-technique detail (green = at least one rule, red = blind spot)</summary>
    {% for tactic, buckets in coverage_groups.items() %}
    <h3>{{ tactic }}</h3>
    <div class="chips">
      {% for entry in buckets.covered %}
      <span class="chip ok" title="{{ entry.technique.name }}: {{ entry.rule_count }} rule(s)">{{ entry.technique.id }}</span>
      {% endfor %}
      {% for entry in buckets.uncovered %}
      <span class="chip miss" title="{{ entry.technique.name }}: no rules">{{ entry.technique.id }}</span>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </details>

  {% if summary.unknown_technique_ids %}
  <h2>Rule tags not in this ATT&amp;CK release</h2>
  <p class="sub">{{ summary.unknown_technique_ids | join(", ") }}. Deprecated or unknown in the
  loaded bundle; excluded from the coverage counts.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="footer">
    Generated by Bastion, a defensive detection engine. It reads logs you own and recognizes
    traces of known techniques; it never attacks anything. This page is self-contained and makes
    no network requests.
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
